      "title": "MCQ Practice",
      "type": "mcq",
      "items": [
        {
          "question": "Why was Ronnie angry and disappointed? (You may choose more than one option.)",
          "options": "(a) The guard had stopped him.    (b) He was hungry.    (c) He felt that he was the best child and should get the basket.",
          "answer": "(a) The guard had stopped him.",
          "sources": {
            "textbook": true
          }
        },
        {
          "question": "How did Ronnie react when he saw the basket of chocolates at the gate?",
          "options": "(a) 😮 Surprised    (b) 🤔 Thinking    (c) 😔 Sad",
          "answer": "(a) 😮 Surprised",
          "sources": {
            "textbook": true
          }
        },
        {
          "question": "“Never give up, try again.” What did Ronnie's mother mean by saying this?",
          "options": "(a) Never feel that you can't do something. Go back and try again.    (b) Give everything to others.    (c) If you can't do something, don't do it.",
          "answer": "(a) Never feel that you can't do something. Go back and try again.",
          "sources": {
            "textbook": true
          }
        },
        {
          "question": "What did Ronnie's mother advise him to do to get into the house?",
          "options": "(a) shout at the guard    (b) politely ask the guard to open the gate    (c) break the lock on the gate",
          "answer": "(b) politely ask the guard to open the gate",
          "sources": {
            "textbook": true
          }
        },
        {
          "question": "A: Ronnie did not ask the guard politely to open the gate. B: The guard did not let Ronnie in because he was ill-mannered. Which is correct?",
          "options": "(a) Both A and B are true and B explains A.    (b) Both A and B are true but B doesn't explain A.    (c) A is false and B is true.",
          "answer": "(a) Both A and B are true and B explains A.",
          "sources": {
            "textbook": true
          }
        }
      ]
