    {
      "title": "Grammar Notes",
      "type": "block",
      "items": [
        {
          "heading": "Pronouns",
          "lines": [
            "A pronoun is a word that is used in place of a noun.",
            "Examples: I, we, he, she, him, her, they",
            "'It' is used for non-living things and animals when we do not know whether it is male or female."
          ],
          "sources": {
            "textbook": true
          }
        },
        {
          "heading": "Articles",
          "lines": [
            "A is used with singular number and before consonant sounds. Examples: a boy, a bag",
            "An is used with singular number and before vowel (a, e, i, o, u) sounds. Examples: an apple, an onion",
            "Hint: it is the sound that matters and not the letter.",
            "",
            "The is a definite article. We use it before the names of a particular person, place or thing. Examples: the Qutub Minar, the Ganga"
          ],
          "sources": {
            "textbook": true
          }
        }
      ]
    },
